From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] SystemUI: system bars that always look the same

Status bar and navigation bar take their background and the colour of their
icons from the window below: transparent over a window that draws behind
them, light or dark icons as it asks. Every change of application then
repaints both bars, and a bar over a window that asks for nothing is white
icons on black.

On e-paper each such repaint is a slow update that leaves traces, and the
stock reader's bars are black on white throughout. With
config_opaqueSystemBars=true both bars always have their opaque background
(system_bar_background_opaque, as BarTransitions.setAlwaysOpaque() already
does for the car navigation bar), and the icons are dark if that colour is
light, light if it is dark.

